// delete_workdrive_file.dg — best-effort delete-by-id for a WorkDrive file, used by the pipeline's
// self-cleanup: every call site passes in a resource_id the pipeline itself just finished using
// (a superseded digest_run file, a consumed batch-state file, a consumed batch-results relay
// file), never an id sourced from anywhere else — so this never risks touching the permanent
// house-rules files (Digest_house_rules_<profile>_file_id), whose ids never flow through this
// function.
//
// No native zoho.workdrive.deleteFile task exists (same absence ../shared/fetch_workdrive_text.dg's
// header already confirmed for a native downloadFile task) — this goes through WorkDrive's REST API
// via invokeurl instead, same connection ("workdrive_connection") as every other WorkDrive call in
// this repo. A plain DELETE to /api/v1/files/<id> was tried first and rejected live with 415
// (Unsupported Media Type) — WorkDrive doesn't delete this way. The confirmed approach, per
// WorkDrive's own API docs: PATCH /api/v1/files/<id> with a JSON:API body setting
// attributes.status to "61" (trash) moves the file to WorkDrive's trash rather than purging it
// immediately — an acceptable, arguably preferable, first behavior for a cleanup job (reversible
// if this ever deletes something it shouldn't have).
//
// Never throws — a failed cleanup should not break the nightly digest run itself (same
// last-good-stays philosophy as the per-user catch blocks in generate/digest_generate.dg /
// generate/digest_finish_batches.dg). Logs and swallows any error instead.

String standalone.deleteWorkdriveFile(String fileId)
{
	if (fileId == null || fileId == "") {
		return "skipped — empty fileId";
	}
	try {
		attributes = Map();
		attributes.put("status", "61");
		data = Map();
		data.put("attributes", attributes);
		data.put("type", "files");
		body = Map();
		body.put("data", data);

		headers = Map();
		headers.put("Accept", "application/vnd.api+json");

		response = invokeurl
		[
			url: "https://www.zohoapis.com/workdrive/api/v1/files/" + fileId
			type: PATCH
			parameters: body.toString()
			headers: headers
			connection: "workdrive_connection"
		];
		info response;
		r= "deleted";
	} catch (e) {
		info "deleteWorkdriveFile: failed to delete " + fileId + ": " + e;
		r= "failed: " + e;
	}
	return r;
}
